}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions:<span class=\"bullet\">Proofread the sentence.</span>\n<span class=\"bullet\">Click on the incorrect word.</span>\n<span class=\"bullet\">Type in the correct word to complete the sentence. </span> <span class=\"bullet\">Use capital letters where necessary.</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": 2, "type": "template_override"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}]}], "type": "GIW", "template_override": 2}, {"id": 11, "stimuli_ids": [], "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "responses": [{"id": 0, "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, {"id": 1, "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}], "type": "RSLT", "template_override": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Strange Stories", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Island of Rabbits", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Relate information about common solutions to problems.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect Tense vs. Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect</span>: ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "</li><li>For something that started in the past and continues in the present. </li></ul> Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> I have studied English since 2014.</span> <br><br> </li><li>For something that has been done several times. </li></ul>Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">I have read this book four times. </span> <br> <br></li><li>For experiences up to the present. </li></ul> Example: <br><span class=\"italic\"> This is the best trip I've ever had.</span> <br><br></li><li> For something that happened in the past but is relevant at the time of speaking. </li></ul>  Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> I can't call her. I've lost my cellphone. </span> <br> <br> </li><li>For referring to a time that is not yet finished. </li></ul> Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Have you seen Richard today?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\"> Simple Past </span>for: <br></li><li>  Something that was finished at a certain period of time. </li></ul>  Example: <br>  <span class=\"italic\">I saw Richard yesterday. </span> <br> <span class=\"italic\">I finished my project two hours ago. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sentence\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Between 1929 and 1945 the island was home to the Japanese army. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" between 1929 and 1945\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">It just appeared to disappear! </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" at the time previously mentioned\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> The poison gas factory has closed down and has been replaced by a museum. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" sometime after the war ended but when is not stated\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> The unfortunate test rabbits are still there and they have grown in number.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" since they were set free sometime in the past \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "It was used to house a secret poison gas factory. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Because of this, the island was removed from Japanese maps. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Today the island has changed.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The military lookout posts that were on the island have fallen into disrepair. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Gerunds and Infinitives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> is a verb ending with -ing (doing).<br/>An <span class=\"strong\">infinitive</span> is to + verb (to do).", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are some verbs that can only be followed by a gerund: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "think about (doing)<br/>imagine (doing)<br/>can't help (doing)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:  <span class=\"italic\"><br/><span class=\"strong\">Imagine walking</span> roaming wooded areas and walking the paths, <span class=\"strong\">being</span> chased by hundreds of wild bunnies! </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You always use a gerund after a phrasal verb.<br/>Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">But all that most day-visitors <span class=\"strong\">think about</span> doing is feeding the feral rabbits.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There are some verbs that can only be followed by an infinitive:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "shocked (to do)<br/>used (to do)<br/>arrange (to do)<br/>appear (to do)<br/>choose (to do)<br/>decide (to do)<br/>be able (to do)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">It was <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> house a secret poison gas factory.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There are some verbs that can be followed by either an infinitive or a gerund with a difference in meaning:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "try (to do):  attempt unsuccessfully<br/>try (doing): experiment by doing different things ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples:<br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">They are trying</span> to get to that food you brought along!</span><br/>(they haven't been successful)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You should <span class=\"strong\">try leaving</span> the bag of food and <span class=\"strong\">moving</span> away from it to lose them.</span><br/>(experiment that way first)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Okunoshima island, I was <span class=\"strong\">shocked to</span> find out, has had a dark past.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You can <span class=\"strong\">arrange to</span> visit this small Japanese island that's only a short trip from the mainland.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The army <span class=\"strong\">chose to</span> use Okunoshima because it has a discreet location and is far from civilian populations. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They <span class=\"strong\">decided to</span> bring rabbits onto the island so that they could test the effects of the poison on them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Visitors to the island can <span class=\"strong\">enjoy swimming</span> in the clean water that surrounds the island. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It just <span class=\"strong\">appeared to</span> disappear! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">can't help thinking</span> how cute they are, even when they are swarming all over you.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about a strange island.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to shock", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cause (someone) to feel surprised and upset", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Okunoshima island, I was shocked to find out, has had a dark past.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "feral", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not domesticated ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Most visitors think about feeding the feral rabbits.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "poison", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that can cause serious harm to the body if consumed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The island was used to house a secret poison gas factory.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gas", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an airlike fluid substance with the ability to expand without limit", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The poison gas factory has closed down.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to remove", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to eliminate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The island was removed from Japanese maps. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "discreet", "type": "name"}, {"content": "careful or tactful in one's conduct or speech", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The army chose to use Okunoshima because it has a discreet location. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to appear", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to seem", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The island just appeared to disappear!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "civilian", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who is not with the military", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The poison gas plant is far from civilian populations.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob01aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "military", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the armed forces", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The military lookout posts that were on the island have fallen into disrepair.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob01aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "lookout post", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a place for a guard or a soldier to keep watch", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The soldier left his lookout post after his shift.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob01aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online or to the library to find out about an interesting island.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find out where it is, what happens there, who goes there and what there is to do. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Explain why it is interesting.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 200 words giving the full information in your own words.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Try to use verb + gerund and verb + infinitive in your writing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your writing to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss your island with them and get their opinion of it as well.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I find out about an interesting island.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write the full information about it in 200 words.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use verb + gerund and verb + infinitive in my writing about the island.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my written piece with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask my partner for his or her opinion of the island.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}